The Test_Vectors files in this package were generated from the reference
implementation. The optimized implementation is packaged as source code and is
not executed by default by this top-level workflow, so this script can run on a
host without AVX support.

Build Requirements:
  - Reference implementation: ISO C compiler and GNU Make
  - Optimized implementation: GCC or Clang with C23 and C++20 support
  - Optimized target: x86-64 with AES-NI, PCLMULQDQ, and AVX2 support
  - The optimized code may also use VAES, AVX-512, and SHA-NI when available

Implementation directories:
  Reference_Implementation/ - portable ISO C implementation
  Optimized_Implementation/ - optimized x86-64 AVX implementation

Optimized NGCC API layout:
  Each optimized instance keeps the standard KAT_SIG.c driver. KAT_SIG.c
  includes SIG_AlgorithmInstance.h, while the per-instance parameter binding is
  provided by SIG_AlgorithmInstance.h and SIG_AlgorithmInstance.cpp.

KAT generation:
  The final Test_Vectors directory is populated from Reference_Implementation.
